gh-tui — GitHub in a TUI

  gh-tui             Opens interactive menu with live preview pane

  Top-level menu provides access to:
    Pull Requests     List, filter, create, manage PRs (gpr)
    CI / Actions      Workflow status, logs, rerun (gha-ui)
    Secrets           Repo & environment secrets (ghsecrets)
    Environments      Create, configure, delete (ghenv)
    Branches          Rulesets, required checks, defaults (ghbranch)

  The preview pane shows live data as you navigate:
    Hover "Pull Requests" → see open PR titles + status
    Hover "CI / Actions"  → see workflow pass/fail for HEAD
    Hover "Branches"      → see branch list with protection status

  All individual commands still work as standalone shortcuts.

GitHub Actions — CI/CD observability + log viewer

  gha             Show workflow status for current HEAD commit
                  Displays: name, pass/fail/running, link

  gha-fail        Same as gha but filtered to failures only
                  Quick way to see what broke

  gha-open        Opens the Actions tab in your browser
                  Fallback when you need the full GitHub UI

  gha-ui          Interactive workflow picker with action menu
                  Choose scope: current HEAD or recent runs.
                  Pick a workflow, then choose:

    📋 Smart log view
       Shows all steps with status, duration, and dot-fill alignment.
       Passing steps are COLLAPSED (header only).
       Failed steps are AUTO-EXPANDED with their full log output
       shown inline beneath the step header, bordered with │.
       Summary line shows pass/fail/skip counts.
       Output goes through less for scrolling.
       After scrolling: r to refresh (re-fetches), -/q to go back.

    🔍 Browse steps interactively
       fzf list of all steps with ✅/❌/⏭ status.
       Preview pane shows that step's log output as you arrow
       through — no need to select first. ENTER opens the full
       log in less. esc returns to the step list.
       After exiting: r to refresh (re-fetches), -/q to go back.

    🌐 Open in browser
       Falls back to the GitHub Actions UI

    🔁 Rerun this workflow
       Triggers a rerun of the selected workflow

  Navigation (consistent across all interactive commands):
    Menus:  ↑↓ navigate  enter select  -/q back  (like nvim)
    Lists:  type to search  enter select  esc back
    Pagers: r refresh  -/q back

  Your prompt also shows CI status on the right side:
    [5/5 ✅ 1d]  = 5 of 5 passed, last run 1 day ago
    [3/5 ❌ 2h]  = 3 of 5 passed (failures), 2 hours ago
    [5/5 ⏳ now]  = workflows still running


gpr — interactive PR management

  gpr              Filter picker → list PRs → pick one → action menu
                   Filters: all open, needs my review, my PRs,
                   recently closed, recently merged
  gpr create       Create a new PR from current branch
  gpr mine         Show only PRs you authored (shortcut)

  The PR list shows: number, review status, title, author,
  branch, changes (+/-), and date. The preview pane (right side)
  shows full PR details as you navigate.

  After selecting a PR, you get an action menu:

    👁  View details        Full PR info in terminal
    📥 Checkout locally     Switch to the PR's branch
    📝 View diff            Colored diff in pager
    📊 View file changes    Browse individual changed files
    💬 Add comment          Inline or open your editor
    ✅ Approve              With optional message
    🔄 Request changes      Opens editor for feedback
    🏷  Manage labels        Add/remove from available labels
    👤 Request reviewers    Pick from collaborators
    ✏️  Edit title/body      Rename or rewrite description
    🔀 Merge                Pick strategy (squash/merge/rebase)
    ❌ Close PR             Close without merging
    🌐 Open in browser      Fallback to GitHub UI
    🔍 View CI checks       See pass/fail status

  Most actions loop back to the menu so you can do multiple
  things without re-running the command.


ghsecrets — manage repository & environment secrets

  ghsecrets        Opens interactive secrets screen

  Menu options:
    🔑 List repo secrets            Names + last updated (values hidden)
    ➕ Set repo secret              Prompts for name, then secure value input
    🗑  Delete repo secret           Pick from list, confirm delete
    🌍 List environment secrets     Pick env first, then see its secrets
    ➕ Set environment secret       Pick env, then name + value
    🗑  Delete environment secret    Pick env, pick secret, confirm

  Important: GitHub NEVER reveals secret values — not even via API.
  You can set, list (names only), and delete. If you need to see
  a value, you must re-set it.

  Secret names are auto-uppercased (GitHub convention).

  Navigation: -/q back  │  r refresh on list views



ghbranch — branches & rulesets

  ghbranch         Opens interactive branch screen

  Menu options:
    📋 List branches                Shows all with 🛡 for ruled branches
    🛡  View effective rules        What actually governs a branch, across
                                    every ruleset targeting it — plus the
                                    bypass list, which decides whether any
                                    of it is a wall or just guidance
    📜 Manage rulesets              Pick a ruleset, then:
                                      • Enforcement (active/evaluate/disabled)
                                      • Require branches up to date (strict)
                                      • Required checks — add/remove, picked
                                        from names CI actually reported
                                      • Bypass mode (pull_request/always)
    🗑  Delete remote branch         With safety check (won't delete default)
    ⭐ Set default branch            Change repo's default branch
    ⚠️  Legacy classic protection    Read + delete only, for migrating off it

  Rulesets, not classic branch protection. The classic API 404s on a repo
  protected by a ruleset, which is how the old version managed to call main
  protected on one screen and unprotected on the next.

  Nothing here creates a classic rule — a branch with both is a branch where
  "why was this rejected" has two possible answers.

  Writes need admin. Rulesets update with PUT, not PATCH (PATCH 404s and
  looks like a permissions error).

  Navigation: -/q back  │  r refresh on list views

ghenv — environment management

  ghenv            Opens interactive environment screen

  Menu options:
    📋 List environments            Names + creation dates
    🔍 View environment details     Protection rules + secrets
    ➕ Create environment           Just name it
    ⏱  Set wait timer               Delay before deployment (minutes)
    👤 Set required reviewers       Pick from collaborators or type username
    🗑  Delete environment           Removes env AND all its secrets

  Environments are used for deployment targets (staging, production).
  Each can have its own secrets, wait timers, and required reviewers.

  Navigation: -/q back  │  r refresh on list views
  Depends on: gh, fzf, jq
